### Normalized scores (1–100)

**Tool use: 86/100.** Estimated based on pro tier performance and OpenAI's strong agentic capabilities. Caps: strong but not top-tier; comparable to similar-tier pro models.

**Reasoning: 88/100.** Estimated based on rank ~30-45 on AI Intelligence Index for pro tier. Comparison: Claude Opus 5.5 (58), GPT-6 Astra (53). Caps: good reasoning but below flagship models.

**Context window: 95/100.** ~1M tokens typical for Pro tier. Caps: good but not the highest; suitable for long documents and RAG.

**Multimodal: 95/100.** Text + image input, text output. 1M context supports documents and images. Caps: standard multimodal for pro models.

**Coding: 87/100.** Estimated based on pro tier coding capabilities and OpenAI's reputation. Caps: strong coding but not specialized.

**Cost efficiency: 75/100.** Estimated $3-5/M input, $15-25/M output. 80-90% cache discount. Competitive pricing for pro tier. Caps: good value for money.

**Overall Score: 88/100.** Mean of Tool (86) + Reasoning (88) + Context (95) + Multimodal (95) + Coding (87) = 89.2. Solid pro model with good performance and competitive pricing; good all-rounder for general-purpose work.

